WEBVTT

00:26.192 --> 00:27.318
Ms. Kiryu.

00:27.402 --> 00:28.361
Please sign this.

00:28.445 --> 00:29.446
Okay.

00:37.579 --> 00:39.581
You look like you don't get it at all.

00:39.664 --> 00:41.458
-No, I'll check it.
-Thank you.

00:41.541 --> 00:43.752
This too, please.
April's post-mortem reports.

00:43.835 --> 00:45.754
And here is the summary
of the test results.

00:46.337 --> 00:47.172
Got it.

00:47.255 --> 00:48.840
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:49.424 --> 00:51.176
Will you really be okay?

00:51.259 --> 00:52.886
Yes, it's no problem at all.

00:52.969 --> 00:53.928
Of course it isn't.

00:54.012 --> 00:56.514
Ms. Kiryu is the head of MEJ, after all.

00:56.598 --> 00:57.557
Right?

00:57.640 --> 00:58.641
Yes.

01:01.728 --> 01:03.688
Here is the summary
of the chemical analysis.

01:03.772 --> 01:05.065
Please sign it.

01:10.820 --> 01:12.530
I'm going to step out for a bit.

01:12.614 --> 01:15.075
My boss at the Ministry of Health
is calling for me.

01:16.534 --> 01:18.244
-She ran away.
-She certainly did.

01:22.749 --> 01:26.461
Regarding that youth poverty support
project you were moving forward with,

01:26.544 --> 01:28.087
it is finally ready to launch.

01:28.171 --> 01:29.297
What?

01:29.380 --> 01:30.423
Really?

01:30.507 --> 01:33.676
However, since you are busy
with the MEJ now,

01:33.760 --> 01:36.638
I have decided to put
another person in charge of it.

01:36.721 --> 01:37.555
What?

01:37.639 --> 01:39.349
Keep up the good work over there.

01:57.784 --> 01:58.827
Is something wrong?

01:58.910 --> 01:59.869
Well…

01:59.953 --> 02:02.831
It seems your hands have stopped moving.

02:03.706 --> 02:05.708
Oh, yes, they have.

02:06.584 --> 02:10.296
I'm just stamping seals. I'll be fine.
I'll finish it after this all-nighter.

02:10.380 --> 02:12.048
I wouldn't recommend that.

02:12.132 --> 02:14.509
Staying up all night
is the same as being drunk.

02:15.385 --> 02:16.219
Drunk?

02:16.302 --> 02:18.972
Cognitive function
after 24 hours without sleep

02:19.055 --> 02:22.600
is reportedly at the same level
as a blood alcohol concentration

02:22.684 --> 02:24.102
of 0.10 percent.

02:24.185 --> 02:27.522
Information cannot be retained
by the brain in that state.

02:27.605 --> 02:29.566
But I won't finish unless I work
all night.

02:29.649 --> 02:33.194
That said, research shows that women
who sleep for less than four hours

02:33.278 --> 02:36.573
have twice the mortality risk
compared to sleeping seven hours.

02:36.656 --> 02:39.909
By pulling an all-nighter,
you think you're increasing your time,

02:39.993 --> 02:43.746
but you might actually be decreasing it.

02:45.748 --> 02:47.292
I will be careful.

02:47.375 --> 02:48.459
As much as I can.

02:48.543 --> 02:49.377
Okay then!

02:54.215 --> 02:55.216
Hello.

02:55.300 --> 02:56.384
Good evening.

02:56.467 --> 02:58.219
It happened in the owner's room.

02:58.303 --> 02:59.470
This way.

03:02.599 --> 03:04.851
The victim is 39-year-old Hayato Kuriyama.

03:04.934 --> 03:06.311
The owner of this club.

03:06.394 --> 03:10.273
A host from a partner club found the body
when he came for a meeting.

03:17.822 --> 03:21.409
Fine white froth is visible
around the nose and mouth.

03:21.492 --> 03:23.620
There is a possibility of drowning.

03:23.703 --> 03:24.537
Drowning?

03:24.621 --> 03:27.373
You mean he drowned inside a closet?

03:27.457 --> 03:30.710
It would be difficult to kill him outside
and move him here.

03:30.793 --> 03:33.254
But drowning inside a room?

03:33.338 --> 03:36.758
It is possible as long as there is enough
water to cover the mouth and nose.

03:45.350 --> 03:48.811
The autopsy shows
that the cause of death was drowning.

03:48.895 --> 03:50.146
Components of the cleaning agent

03:50.230 --> 03:52.982
used in the room's toilet were
detected in the water inside the lungs.

03:53.066 --> 03:57.237
We found pressure marks on the neck
and a slight bruise on the head.

03:57.320 --> 03:58.947
Both occurred while he was alive.

03:59.030 --> 04:00.907
We also found skin fragments

04:00.990 --> 04:03.159
under his fingernails
that don't belong to Mr. Kuriyama.

04:03.243 --> 04:04.452
Testing revealed

04:04.994 --> 04:07.538
that it is female DNA.

04:09.457 --> 04:10.917
Female…

04:11.000 --> 04:14.295
Did the victim
have any trouble with women?

04:14.379 --> 04:17.590
When he took a liking to a girl,
he would try to keep her for himself.

04:17.674 --> 04:19.300
They were too scared to refuse.

04:19.384 --> 04:21.469
Some girls were backed into a corner.

04:21.552 --> 04:24.347
Had he been clashing
with anyone in particular lately?

04:30.019 --> 04:31.229
Well, actually,

04:32.230 --> 04:35.066
one girl was arguing with him
about breaking up.

04:41.781 --> 04:42.991
Excuse me.

04:44.325 --> 04:45.410
Police.

04:48.538 --> 04:49.706
Police?

04:49.789 --> 04:53.126
Could you come with us to the station
to discuss Hayato Kuriyama?

04:53.209 --> 04:54.794
I'm sorry.

04:54.877 --> 04:57.422
I have to go to work now.

04:58.089 --> 05:01.634
Female DNA was detected on the body.

05:11.811 --> 05:15.815
Will you cooperate with a DNA test?

05:21.988 --> 05:23.448
I'm sorry.

05:27.327 --> 05:29.120
I'm sorry.

05:31.998 --> 05:33.458
The culprit is 24-year-old

05:33.541 --> 05:35.626
Miyuki Yanagihara,
an employee at the club.

05:35.710 --> 05:39.547
She visited the victim's room
on the day of the crime.

05:40.131 --> 05:42.008
Please just let me go.

05:45.178 --> 05:46.804
I'm at my limit.

05:56.105 --> 05:57.565
I'll kill you if you run away.

06:27.136 --> 06:29.764
She put poison in his protein shake
and left the room.

06:30.681 --> 06:31.641
However…

06:31.724 --> 06:33.142
Where's your earring?

06:33.226 --> 06:34.060
What?

06:37.772 --> 06:38.689
One second.

07:28.489 --> 07:31.868
So then, she strangled the victim
after he regained consciousness.

07:36.539 --> 07:39.750
After that,
fearing he would wake up again,

07:39.834 --> 07:41.836
she submerged his face in the toilet.

07:48.634 --> 07:49.719
What?

07:49.802 --> 07:52.889
But no poison was detected
in the autopsy, was it?

07:52.972 --> 07:55.892
The components checked
in the initial screening are limited.

07:55.975 --> 08:00.521
Irregular toxins won't be detected
unless we specifically test for them.

08:00.605 --> 08:01.439
Test for them?

08:01.522 --> 08:04.066
What was the substance used?

08:04.692 --> 08:08.237
She's actually remaining silent
about the poison.

08:08.905 --> 08:10.114
What poison was it?

08:11.365 --> 08:13.075
Where did you get it?

08:16.537 --> 08:18.080
I forgot.

08:18.164 --> 08:19.207
What?

08:19.290 --> 08:20.374
Why?

08:21.167 --> 08:22.919
Maybe she's protecting someone.

08:23.002 --> 08:26.255
In that case, finding the toxin
could be quite difficult.

08:26.339 --> 08:29.634
For now, let's broaden
the scope of the analysis.

08:29.717 --> 08:30.843
-Okay.
-Okay.

08:30.927 --> 08:33.679
We will investigate
the source of procurement as well.

08:36.265 --> 08:37.099
Hello?

08:38.976 --> 08:40.603
Huh? What do you mean?

08:43.606 --> 08:44.649
I'll be right back.

08:46.776 --> 08:47.818
What happened?

08:49.111 --> 08:51.531
A staff member from the club
turned himself in.

08:54.200 --> 08:57.119
He says he was the one
who killed the owner.

09:04.710 --> 09:06.671
I'm the one who did it.

09:07.255 --> 09:10.091
That day, I went
to talk to him about a loan.

09:10.591 --> 09:11.801
Please, I beg you!

09:12.426 --> 09:14.011
Are you stupid?

09:20.643 --> 09:21.811
Bastard!

09:35.408 --> 09:37.910
After that, I got scared

09:37.994 --> 09:39.412
and ran away.

09:40.037 --> 09:44.125
But then I saw on the news
that Miyuki had been arrested.

09:44.875 --> 09:46.335
It was all my fault.

09:47.461 --> 09:49.380
Miyuki is innocent.

09:49.463 --> 09:51.257
Please, arrest me now!

09:51.340 --> 09:52.383
Mr. Murano.

09:53.467 --> 09:56.846
Did you really kill him by strangulation?

09:57.638 --> 09:58.598
Yes.

10:02.143 --> 10:04.604
She has already admitted to the crime.

10:04.687 --> 10:07.189
That's impossible! Please, investigate!

10:07.273 --> 10:08.274
Like I said…

10:08.357 --> 10:10.234
Where is the ashtray you used to hit him?

10:10.318 --> 10:11.360
Hey.

10:12.069 --> 10:13.613
I threw it into the Ooguri River.

10:17.491 --> 10:19.577
Why did you ask about the murder weapon?

10:19.660 --> 10:22.246
The bruise on the top of the victim's head

10:22.330 --> 10:25.625
might have been caused
by Murano hitting him.

10:25.708 --> 10:29.086
If we find the weapon and match it,
we can be certain.

10:29.170 --> 10:33.841
Wasn't that just from bumping into
something when dragging him around?

10:33.924 --> 10:36.302
Besides, the cause of death
was drowning, right?

10:36.385 --> 10:40.598
Murano's statement
that he strangled him doesn't add up.

10:40.681 --> 10:43.809
It's only natural to consider
Miyuki Yanagihara as the culprit.

10:43.893 --> 10:47.938
Murano is just giving a false confession
to protect Miyuki Yanagihara.

10:48.022 --> 10:49.440
Miyuki is innocent.

10:49.523 --> 10:51.150
Please, arrest me now!

10:51.233 --> 10:54.153
However, as long as
no poison has been detected,

10:54.236 --> 10:57.114
we should investigate
assuming every possibility.

10:57.198 --> 11:00.660
Let's investigate their relationship and
search for the murder weapon.

11:00.743 --> 11:02.662
-Supervisor.
-Yes?

11:02.745 --> 11:05.498
The cause of death
has been determined to be drowning.

11:05.581 --> 11:08.876
There's no need for the MEJ
to investigate any further, is there?

11:09.835 --> 11:11.671
Oh, well…

11:12.797 --> 11:15.883
The MEJ has the authority to conduct
all general investigations to--

11:15.966 --> 11:18.260
Do you have anything else
besides "authority"?

11:19.011 --> 11:21.430
How can you call yourself the supervisor?

11:23.057 --> 11:24.016
Let's go.

11:24.100 --> 11:24.934
Yes, ma'am!

11:28.521 --> 11:31.357
We have no choice but to move on our own.

11:32.441 --> 11:36.278
Could you investigate the relationship
between Yanagihara and Murano?

11:36.862 --> 11:38.739
What? Me?

11:38.823 --> 11:41.492
I will proceed
with identifying the poison.

11:41.575 --> 11:43.244
I'm counting on you.

11:53.170 --> 11:54.880
Are we looking for it after all?

11:54.964 --> 11:58.217
We were told the weapon was thrown away,
so we have no choice.

11:59.468 --> 12:01.387
Here I thought I could go home today.

12:01.470 --> 12:03.347
I wanted to finish early too.

12:03.431 --> 12:04.849
Do you have any plans?

12:04.932 --> 12:06.183
I do.

12:06.267 --> 12:07.393
I'm getting snacks,

12:07.476 --> 12:10.479
watch a reality-TV show
while drinking wine, and doze off.

12:10.563 --> 12:12.690
Wait. Ms. Dojima, you watch dating shows?

12:13.274 --> 12:14.191
I do.

12:14.275 --> 12:17.987
Wow, you're actually interested in love
and things like that?

12:20.072 --> 12:23.576
Even I have interests in things
that aren't violent and terrible.

12:39.175 --> 12:40.176
We're taking a break!

12:40.259 --> 12:41.719
We're taking a break.

12:49.727 --> 12:52.188
I mean, how long are we going to do this?

12:54.148 --> 12:56.692
The culprit is Miyuki Yanagihara.

12:56.775 --> 12:59.153
We're not going to find that ash tray!

13:01.614 --> 13:04.366
Something's bothering me.

13:05.034 --> 13:08.454
Nothing came up in the gas chromatography
or liquid chromatography.

13:08.954 --> 13:11.332
Capillary chromatography is also negative.

13:12.374 --> 13:13.542
Damn it!

13:14.251 --> 13:17.046
We'd have no trouble
if she just said what it was.

13:17.129 --> 13:18.839
I wonder why she won't.

13:18.923 --> 13:21.550
Maybe that club staff member
got it for her.

13:22.510 --> 13:25.804
I think she's staying silent
to protect him.

13:25.888 --> 13:28.599
So they're both covering for each other?

13:28.682 --> 13:29.475
Exactly.

13:29.558 --> 13:33.646
Is there a possibility that there was
no poison in the first place?

13:33.729 --> 13:36.398
Kuriyama had pulmonary edema.

13:36.482 --> 13:41.195
While it's a finding seen in drowning,
it can also occur in drug poisoning.

13:41.820 --> 13:45.991
We cannot deny the possibility that
some kind of drug was ingested.

13:47.159 --> 13:48.994
I'm asking again.

13:49.662 --> 13:52.289
How did you get the poison?

13:54.875 --> 13:56.794
Why won't you tell me?

14:01.674 --> 14:04.426
You're protecting someone, aren't you?

14:05.970 --> 14:06.929
A lover…

14:08.472 --> 14:09.390
perhaps?

14:15.563 --> 14:20.484
Were Miyuki and Murano possibly
dating in secret, without telling anyone?

14:20.568 --> 14:22.862
No, I can't imagine they were.

14:23.821 --> 14:25.531
The owner would have them killed.

14:27.408 --> 14:30.244
When did Miyuki start working at the club?

14:30.828 --> 14:32.454
About a year ago, I think.

14:32.538 --> 14:34.957
She had money problems
and was looking for a new job.

14:35.040 --> 14:37.918
What kind of person was Murano?

14:38.002 --> 14:39.587
He was actually a former host.

14:39.670 --> 14:43.340
He was working at an affiliate club
and moved here.

14:43.424 --> 14:45.718
Do you know the name of that host club?

14:49.263 --> 14:50.681
Supervisor!

14:51.390 --> 14:52.308
Why are you here?

14:53.601 --> 14:55.895
To interview involved parties.

14:55.978 --> 14:57.438
Without telling the police?

14:57.521 --> 14:58.856
It was Dr. Masumi's instruction.

14:58.939 --> 15:01.317
You just do whatever
people tell you, don't you?

15:01.400 --> 15:02.484
Excuse me.

15:07.323 --> 15:08.616
A host club?

15:09.575 --> 15:11.410
So that's your hobby?

15:12.161 --> 15:14.997
No! It's Murano's former workplace.

15:15.664 --> 15:17.666
I thought I might learn something.

15:22.838 --> 15:24.465
Are you coming?

15:24.548 --> 15:25.382
What?

15:26.175 --> 15:29.345
You'll just move around secretly
on your own anyway, right?

15:32.514 --> 15:35.392
Murano was a good guy.
He wasn't suited to being a host.

15:35.476 --> 15:38.520
Had you heard anything from Murano?

15:38.604 --> 15:41.065
About trouble with the owner,

15:41.148 --> 15:44.401
or about a hostess
named Miyuki Yanagihara?

15:46.153 --> 15:48.405
I'm not sure.

15:51.951 --> 15:53.035
It's 100,000?

15:53.118 --> 15:55.621
-One of those then.
-What?

15:55.704 --> 15:58.082
Champagne coming up!

15:58.165 --> 16:00.250
Thank you, welcome to the club!

16:00.334 --> 16:02.044
-Welcome!
-Welcome!

16:02.127 --> 16:03.253
All right!

16:03.837 --> 16:05.047
Thanks.

16:06.715 --> 16:08.592
What? Aren't the police
supposed to pay this?

16:08.676 --> 16:11.845
You're the supervisor, right?
Figure it out with your budget.

16:13.514 --> 16:16.767
Want to go get food?
I'll at least make that my treat.

16:18.310 --> 16:19.645
Let's go.

16:25.275 --> 16:27.361
NO DRUGS TARGETED FOR SCREENING DETECTED

16:35.119 --> 16:38.163
Getting a hostess job
because of financial trouble, huh?

16:38.247 --> 16:42.209
Many young people can't earn enough
even if they work full-time

16:42.292 --> 16:45.045
due to non-regular employment
and low wages.

16:45.129 --> 16:47.631
So they end up in the nightlife business.

16:47.715 --> 16:49.508
You're surprisingly well-informed.

16:49.591 --> 16:51.927
Originally, I wanted to
work in social welfare

16:52.011 --> 16:54.471
because I wanted to help those people.

16:54.555 --> 16:56.098
Before coming to MEJ,

16:56.181 --> 16:58.809
I was in youth poverty support
for a long time.

16:59.560 --> 17:02.896
Why is someone as noble as you
the MEJ supervisor?

17:02.980 --> 17:06.358
Poverty support and
the cause of death are totally different.

17:12.990 --> 17:14.366
You got transferred.

17:16.785 --> 17:17.619
Yes.

17:21.457 --> 17:25.210
Of course, I intend to work
as hard as I can in any way I can.

17:26.628 --> 17:27.838
But, to be honest,

17:28.714 --> 17:31.050
I still want to return to the MHLW.

17:35.637 --> 17:37.222
That might be perfect, actually.

17:37.765 --> 17:38.682
What?

17:39.475 --> 17:43.145
If you've done that kind of work,
don't you understand how she feels?

17:43.979 --> 17:44.855
You know,

17:45.481 --> 17:47.858
she has stopped talking to the police.

17:49.568 --> 17:51.403
Why don't you try talking to her?

17:57.659 --> 17:59.703
My name is Kiryu from MEJ.

18:01.872 --> 18:03.540
We're an MHLW organization

18:03.624 --> 18:06.001
that specializes in determining
causes of death.

18:07.836 --> 18:09.755
No matter how many times you ask,

18:10.839 --> 18:12.841
I don't remember anything
about the poison.

18:19.723 --> 18:21.225
Are you protecting Murano?

18:23.560 --> 18:24.770
Murano?

18:26.522 --> 18:29.191
What has he got to do with it?

18:30.692 --> 18:31.777
Actually,

18:33.195 --> 18:35.114
Murano turned himself in.

18:39.034 --> 18:39.952
What?

18:48.252 --> 18:52.464
What was your relationship with Murano?

18:54.550 --> 18:55.801
Murano…

18:57.678 --> 18:59.972
was always supporting me.

19:04.101 --> 19:07.354
I started this job
to pay back my student loans.

19:08.605 --> 19:10.315
I've always regretted it.

19:11.984 --> 19:13.193
Student loans?

19:13.986 --> 19:16.113
My family was poor.

19:16.780 --> 19:19.241
I went to a beautician school
on a scholarship.

19:22.161 --> 19:24.997
But the salary
for an assistant was low, so…

19:27.916 --> 19:30.252
I started a part-time job
at a hostess club.

19:31.003 --> 19:32.754
You don't have to worry anymore.

19:34.298 --> 19:37.134
Some girls work only until
they've paid back their scholarships.

19:39.678 --> 19:41.221
Thank you very much.

19:42.389 --> 19:43.599
But in the end,

19:44.391 --> 19:46.143
I was forced to become his mistress.

19:49.396 --> 19:50.856
Before I knew it…

19:52.941 --> 19:54.693
I had nowhere else to go

19:55.611 --> 19:57.529
and no place to return to.

19:58.989 --> 20:02.117
I had no choice
but to rely on that man to live.

20:05.412 --> 20:06.705
And during that time…

20:07.331 --> 20:09.166
I'm here for you.

20:10.500 --> 20:13.128
…Murano encouraged me.

20:14.087 --> 20:16.590
I had to do my best to get out of there…

20:19.134 --> 20:21.595
and started to believe that I could.

20:23.639 --> 20:24.640
But…

20:30.687 --> 20:32.940
How did it end up like this?

20:37.236 --> 20:40.447
So they were dating after all.

20:41.240 --> 20:42.282
Probably.

20:44.034 --> 20:45.118
Also,

20:45.202 --> 20:48.664
it doesn't seem they coordinated
their stories and turned themselves in.

20:48.747 --> 20:50.999
When I told her Murano
had turned himself in,

20:51.083 --> 20:53.710
Miyuki looked genuinely surprised.

20:54.211 --> 20:56.755
It didn't seem like she knew beforehand.

20:57.631 --> 21:01.260
Then Murano really was
protecting Yanagihara?

21:03.470 --> 21:05.681
That might be true.

21:12.980 --> 21:13.814
What's wrong?

21:18.443 --> 21:20.445
My family was poor too,

21:20.946 --> 21:23.699
and I went to university
thanks to a scholarship.

21:24.825 --> 21:27.327
I joined the MHLW

21:27.411 --> 21:31.581
because I wanted to help people
like myself move forward, but…

21:33.125 --> 21:34.501
In my current position,

21:35.294 --> 21:36.670
I can't do anything.

21:42.759 --> 21:44.469
Is that really true?

21:47.723 --> 21:49.266
Even in your current position,

21:49.933 --> 21:51.643
isn't there something you can do?

21:53.186 --> 21:56.189
That's what you worked so hard for
at the Ministry, isn't it?

22:06.616 --> 22:07.743
Also,

22:08.368 --> 22:10.037
there's something bothering me.

22:11.788 --> 22:14.833
When her arm was grabbed by the victim,

22:15.375 --> 22:17.377
he apparently called her "Mari."

22:18.170 --> 22:19.254
Mari?

22:25.886 --> 22:27.012
Mari…

22:27.637 --> 22:28.680
What?

22:30.348 --> 22:31.433
Mari…

22:34.936 --> 22:38.774
To have to depend on someone
who gets your name wrong…

22:40.400 --> 22:43.236
She felt pathetic
for having to live like that.

22:48.116 --> 22:49.618
She said that before she knew it,

22:50.118 --> 22:52.245
she was strangling him.

22:54.414 --> 22:57.084
Maybe she was just at her limit.

22:57.167 --> 22:59.878
The victim laid hands on many women.

22:59.961 --> 23:01.296
She might be one of them.

23:02.964 --> 23:05.634
It might have something
to do with the case.

23:05.717 --> 23:07.260
I'll look into it.

23:23.568 --> 23:24.694
Let's get married.

23:25.987 --> 23:27.114
It's impossible.

23:28.323 --> 23:29.407
We can't escape.

23:33.203 --> 23:35.205
If only he wasn't here,

23:37.457 --> 23:40.127
I could be with the person I love forever.

23:57.144 --> 24:00.272
Even in your current position,
isn't there something you can do?

24:02.107 --> 24:04.609
I had to do my best to get out of there…

24:13.285 --> 24:14.369
All right.

24:24.379 --> 24:25.213
What…

24:27.883 --> 24:29.467
You were working until morning?

24:30.093 --> 24:31.511
As you can see.

24:32.470 --> 24:35.307
So, did you find any poison?

24:35.390 --> 24:36.308
No.

24:37.058 --> 24:39.895
I've tried a thousand patterns,

24:40.437 --> 24:43.523
but the parameter settings
are still infinite.

24:48.945 --> 24:49.863
Yes?

24:49.946 --> 24:51.406
Ms. Dojima, it's an emergency!

24:51.489 --> 24:54.576
The ashtray believed to be
the murder weapon has been found!

24:56.411 --> 24:58.371
The shape of the discovered ashtray

24:58.455 --> 25:00.957
matches the wound on Kuriyama's head.

25:01.041 --> 25:03.168
Murano's fingerprints
were also detected on the ashtray.

25:03.919 --> 25:06.087
What about
Miyuki Yanagihara's fingerprints?

25:06.171 --> 25:07.464
None of hers.

25:07.964 --> 25:11.635
So the culprit really was
Murano after all?

25:11.718 --> 25:12.636
Yes.

25:12.719 --> 25:15.639
The prosecution has also decided
to indict Murano.

25:16.723 --> 25:18.058
Please wait.

25:18.141 --> 25:19.768
The cause of death was drowning.

25:19.851 --> 25:23.104
Murano's statement says
that he strangled him. It doesn't add up.

25:23.188 --> 25:24.648
We know that.

25:25.732 --> 25:28.735
But evidence backing the crime
has surfaced.

25:28.818 --> 25:31.905
According to the police,
it appears that Murano is the culprit.

25:32.405 --> 25:35.116
The investigation task force
is being disbanded.

26:01.476 --> 26:02.727
Wait!

26:39.764 --> 26:42.142
The mystery has not yet been solved.

26:43.810 --> 26:46.354
What poison did Miyuki administer,

26:47.314 --> 26:51.443
and why does Murano's statement
differ from the cause of death?

26:53.987 --> 26:55.739
I'm going to the scene again.

26:56.406 --> 27:00.076
There might be a piece
we haven't found yet.

27:05.915 --> 27:06.750
Okay!

27:12.464 --> 27:14.341
We're going to
Miyuki Yanagihara's apartment.

27:14.424 --> 27:15.550
What?

27:15.633 --> 27:18.887
We can't just let it end
like this either, can we?

27:20.680 --> 27:21.765
Yes, ma'am!

27:46.456 --> 27:47.540
Cute.

27:48.249 --> 27:50.251
Did it belong to the victim, you think?

28:05.266 --> 28:06.559
Hey, you!

28:07.644 --> 28:09.396
-Wait!
-Stop!

28:14.025 --> 28:15.735
Did you find something?

28:16.778 --> 28:19.864
No, nothing in particular.

28:22.867 --> 28:23.952
Doctor,

28:24.035 --> 28:26.246
that pen is bothering you, right?

28:26.329 --> 28:29.791
Compared to the victim's
other belongings, it's quite different.

28:29.874 --> 28:32.419
I wonder why. It's a mystery.

28:32.502 --> 28:33.920
Dr. Masumi,

28:34.003 --> 28:37.465
no toxins were detected
in the line test either.

28:38.049 --> 28:39.509
Okay.

28:39.592 --> 28:42.887
Let's go back to basics and start over
from the elemental analysis.

28:42.971 --> 28:44.097
Okay.

28:45.932 --> 28:46.891
It's Mari-chan!

28:48.101 --> 28:49.060
Mari-chan?

28:49.644 --> 28:50.812
Magical Detective Mari.

28:50.895 --> 28:52.647
It's a new popular anime.

28:52.731 --> 28:53.982
Oh, okay.

28:57.736 --> 29:00.488
Is this girl called "Mari"?

29:01.072 --> 29:01.865
Yes.

29:02.741 --> 29:03.825
Is something wrong?

29:03.908 --> 29:08.204
When the victim woke up,
he apparently called Miyuki "Mari."

29:08.288 --> 29:13.209
The police couldn't find any Mari
who knew the victim.

29:13.293 --> 29:16.921
But surely, it couldn't be
an anime character, right?

29:22.844 --> 29:24.846
I found out the name of the poison.

29:25.555 --> 29:26.723
What is it?

29:28.349 --> 29:29.309
Aconitine.

29:31.478 --> 29:33.396
Of course, we wouldn't find that.

29:33.480 --> 29:35.523
We don't usually test for that.

29:35.607 --> 29:37.442
I'll cross-reference it with the database.

29:37.525 --> 29:38.735
Wait.

29:39.944 --> 29:42.280
We did not find aconitine in the body.

29:44.407 --> 29:46.034
The pieces might be

29:46.868 --> 29:48.536
coming together.

29:56.753 --> 30:00.173
Regarding the poison
you said you gave to Kuriyama,

30:00.256 --> 30:04.010
no matter how much we investigated,
it could not be detected.

30:05.512 --> 30:07.847
However, that was only natural.

30:09.057 --> 30:12.727
Kuriyama had not ingested poison
in the first place.

30:13.978 --> 30:15.730
What do you mean?

30:17.106 --> 30:19.776
I put poison in his drink.

30:19.859 --> 30:24.781
I heard you were called
"Mari" by the victim.

30:25.740 --> 30:27.200
What about it?

30:27.283 --> 30:30.620
Do you know who Mari is?

30:33.164 --> 30:35.834
I don't know.
Just some other woman, right?

30:35.917 --> 30:38.461
I thought so too at first.

30:38.545 --> 30:40.964
But no matter how much we investigated,

30:41.047 --> 30:44.384
we could not find any woman named Mari.

30:45.009 --> 30:47.554
The only Mari found…

30:48.638 --> 30:49.848
was this girl.

30:51.015 --> 30:52.350
From an anime?

30:53.184 --> 30:55.103
Her name is Mari,

30:55.687 --> 30:57.105
from Magical Detective Mari.

30:58.273 --> 31:02.026
Kuriyama was a die-hard fan
of this character.

31:03.236 --> 31:07.448
You're saying I was mistaken
for an anime character?

31:07.532 --> 31:08.491
Yes.

31:09.242 --> 31:11.077
When we examined the hippocampus,

31:11.160 --> 31:13.371
the part of the brain
which governs memory,

31:13.454 --> 31:15.748
we saw necrosis in the surrounding area.

31:15.832 --> 31:16.916
In other words,

31:17.542 --> 31:19.919
Kuriyama suffered
a consciousness disorder,

31:20.003 --> 31:23.715
and as a result,
he mistook you for his beloved Mari.

31:25.174 --> 31:29.095
That's because of the poison, right?

31:29.178 --> 31:30.305
No.

31:30.388 --> 31:33.641
Because the poison you used

31:34.142 --> 31:35.810
was aconitine.

31:39.230 --> 31:43.860
The person who purchased
the poison for you told us.

31:44.444 --> 31:45.278
What?

31:46.988 --> 31:47.989
Of course,

31:48.573 --> 31:51.492
you know who that person is.

31:51.576 --> 31:56.080
You've been silent all this time
to protect him, haven't you?

32:00.501 --> 32:01.920
The one who bought the poison

32:02.712 --> 32:03.755
was the host…

32:06.758 --> 32:07.884
Kaito Miura.

32:07.967 --> 32:10.595
No! I bought it myself!

32:10.678 --> 32:13.681
Kaito Miura has already
admitted his involvement.

32:15.058 --> 32:18.227
I was worried there was evidence left
of me buying that poison,

32:18.311 --> 32:20.855
so I went and checked Miyuki's place.

32:20.939 --> 32:23.858
Does that mean you also had
a grudge against Kuriyama?

32:23.942 --> 32:27.153
He found out I was trying to
go independent and was interfering.

32:27.236 --> 32:30.698
But I only bought the poison,
Miyuki is the one who did it.

32:30.782 --> 32:33.910
I won't be charged with murder, right?

32:36.746 --> 32:38.414
It's not Kaito's fault.

32:40.291 --> 32:41.793
I just asked him.

32:41.876 --> 32:44.170
He has nothing to do with it!

32:44.253 --> 32:48.841
You put the aconitine purchased
by Mr. Miura into the protein.

32:48.925 --> 32:51.511
However, if aconitine is ingested,

32:51.594 --> 32:55.556
brain function is instantly destroyed,
so one would never regain consciousness.

32:55.640 --> 32:57.809
So, a disturbance of consciousness

32:57.892 --> 33:00.645
and mistaking you for Mari,
is not possible.

33:02.021 --> 33:03.690
That doesn't make sense.

33:04.273 --> 33:06.901
Then why did the owner collapse?

33:06.985 --> 33:11.864
That's because Kuriyama
had people trying to kill him twice.

33:12.949 --> 33:14.075
Twice?

33:14.659 --> 33:17.829
That day, another person had visited
the owner's room

33:18.413 --> 33:22.000
between when you mixed the poison
into the drink

33:22.583 --> 33:25.670
and you returning
to retrieve your earring.

33:33.011 --> 33:34.220
It was Murano.

33:36.431 --> 33:37.932
Murano?

33:38.016 --> 33:41.769
He said that he went
to ask the owner to release you.

33:42.895 --> 33:44.731
He confessed just now.

33:44.814 --> 33:46.983
Please let Miyuki go!

33:47.859 --> 33:49.652
Please, I beg you!

33:50.528 --> 33:52.155
Are you stupid?

34:14.510 --> 34:16.054
But,

34:16.137 --> 34:19.140
at that time, Kuriyama was not dead yet.

34:21.726 --> 34:24.937
He lost consciousness
because he was strangled,

34:25.021 --> 34:29.525
and his breathing and pulse
became extremely weak.

34:29.609 --> 34:32.070
It's a so-called state of apparent death.

34:33.446 --> 34:35.490
Kuriyama regained consciousness

34:35.573 --> 34:36.991
exited the closet,

34:37.075 --> 34:39.494
and lost consciousness again.

34:40.411 --> 34:43.414
And then you came in.

34:43.956 --> 34:45.416
Seeing him like that,

34:45.500 --> 34:49.587
you mistakenly thought Kuriyama
had died from drinking the poison.

34:49.670 --> 34:52.381
However, Kuriyama,
who was still breathing,

34:52.465 --> 34:54.717
regained consciousness once more.

34:54.801 --> 34:56.969
And due to the consciousness disorder

34:57.053 --> 34:59.722
caused by the hypoxic state
from being strangled,

34:59.806 --> 35:01.057
he got your name…

35:01.140 --> 35:02.225
Mari…

35:02.308 --> 35:03.726
…wrong.

35:03.810 --> 35:08.773
That pushed you
to lay your hands on Kuriyama.

35:10.066 --> 35:15.863
You and Murano both tried
to kill Kuriyama,

35:15.947 --> 35:18.825
and both of you failed.

35:19.492 --> 35:21.035
However, in the end,

35:21.953 --> 35:24.831
you were the one who completed it.

35:30.253 --> 35:31.712
Ms. Yanagihara,

35:32.296 --> 35:35.842
I am committing you to trial
on suspicion of murder.

35:41.472 --> 35:42.723
What about Murano?

35:43.599 --> 35:45.893
He will be charged with attempted murder.

35:47.770 --> 35:52.275
You hid the fact that you had entered
a relationship with Kaito Miura,

35:52.358 --> 35:56.779
and tried to get Murano
to kill the victim, didn't you?

35:56.863 --> 35:58.447
If only he wasn't here,

35:58.531 --> 36:01.534
I could be with the person I love forever.

36:03.035 --> 36:07.081
But you got tired of Murano
never following through,

36:07.790 --> 36:09.750
so you finally did it yourself.

36:10.918 --> 36:14.046
Yet coincidentally,
Murano followed through

36:14.839 --> 36:17.258
on the same day.

36:20.011 --> 36:22.138
I have a message from Murano.

36:22.972 --> 36:24.974
Please tell Miyuki this.

36:26.684 --> 36:28.186
This is my fault.

36:29.478 --> 36:31.314
I'm so sorry.

36:33.232 --> 36:34.066
But,

36:35.318 --> 36:38.362
let's both atone for our crimes

36:39.113 --> 36:40.198
and get married.

36:42.408 --> 36:44.619
I'll be waiting for her forever.

36:49.123 --> 36:51.250
You might have just been using him,

36:51.334 --> 36:53.461
but he was serious.

37:02.261 --> 37:04.180
Are you kidding me?

37:09.310 --> 37:11.395
Stupid useless man.

37:11.479 --> 37:13.940
Don't get ahead of yourself!

37:14.774 --> 37:20.905
It's because you failed to kill him
that I'm in this mess!

37:27.828 --> 37:28.663
And here…

37:35.544 --> 37:38.464
And here I thought
I could finally get out.

37:48.140 --> 37:49.433
Did you really…

37:52.311 --> 37:53.980
think that?

37:58.985 --> 38:00.444
You killed someone.

38:02.989 --> 38:05.616
Even if you managed to get out of this,

38:09.120 --> 38:10.579
by doing all this,

38:13.291 --> 38:14.875
did you really think

38:16.127 --> 38:17.795
you could move forward?

38:28.222 --> 38:29.307
Move forward?

38:32.893 --> 38:35.062
Why would you assume that?

38:37.064 --> 38:39.191
I never said anything about "forward."

38:41.319 --> 38:46.115
I just wanted to break away from the owner
and be with Kaito forever.

38:47.658 --> 38:49.493
I don't care about the future.

38:50.328 --> 38:53.039
As long as I'm happy now,
that's all that matters.

38:57.335 --> 38:58.919
Someone who's talented,

39:01.380 --> 39:03.591
has a good job,

39:05.760 --> 39:08.220
and lives without any hardship

39:10.514 --> 39:12.975
wouldn't understand my feelings.

39:17.521 --> 39:20.024
I even defaulted on my scholarship

39:20.983 --> 39:24.945
and used all the money I earned for Kaito.

39:31.702 --> 39:33.371
It was fun, though.

40:32.930 --> 40:34.056
I…

40:36.725 --> 40:38.853
didn't see anything.

40:49.572 --> 40:50.865
There are people

40:52.366 --> 40:54.618
in society waiting for help.

40:56.954 --> 41:01.167
I thought I was working for those people.

41:04.545 --> 41:06.255
But it was all just an ideal.

41:08.966 --> 41:11.760
I didn't see anything.

41:15.473 --> 41:18.684
Isn't it a good thing by itself
that you realized that?

41:30.196 --> 41:31.280
Hey.

41:31.947 --> 41:33.949
Your nose is running.

41:41.749 --> 41:42.917
Hey.

41:43.918 --> 41:45.127
You look ugly.

41:51.383 --> 41:53.219
Go on, cry.

42:08.734 --> 42:09.860
Ms. Kiryu.

42:09.944 --> 42:12.530
-Stamp this, please.
-Okay.

42:14.281 --> 42:17.493
Mark them all
as "by the end of today," please.

42:18.702 --> 42:19.870
-Okay.
-Okay.

42:23.582 --> 42:24.583
Wait.

42:25.376 --> 42:26.460
Dr. Honda…

42:29.880 --> 42:33.551
What does this LC-MS mean?

42:33.634 --> 42:34.760
What?

42:35.761 --> 42:38.931
Oh, it's the same as always,
so if you could just stamp it for now,

42:39.014 --> 42:39.890
No.

42:40.683 --> 42:41.934
As the supervisor,

42:42.017 --> 42:44.645
I want to really understand it
before I stamp it.

42:44.728 --> 42:45.771
Please tell me.

42:49.358 --> 42:50.734
Can't be helped…

42:51.318 --> 42:54.321
-I'm busy, you know?
-I'm sorry.

42:54.989 --> 42:56.740
Well, simply put,

42:56.824 --> 43:02.162
it means separating components
with LC and analyzing the mass.

43:03.622 --> 43:04.957
Analyzing mass?

43:05.040 --> 43:06.000
Yes.

43:06.083 --> 43:08.460
You mean like on a scale?

43:08.544 --> 43:09.587
No, like I said…

43:10.296 --> 43:11.297
More documents?

43:12.089 --> 43:13.132
For LC-MS,

43:13.215 --> 43:15.384
I recommend this book.

43:16.385 --> 43:17.428
Thank you very much.

43:19.930 --> 43:22.641
LC… Liquid Chromatography?

43:23.642 --> 43:25.102
So what is LC-MS?

43:25.185 --> 43:27.521
It's that instrument over there.

43:35.988 --> 43:39.158
A child suspected of being abused
was in an accident.

43:39.241 --> 43:40.409
What kind of screaming?

43:40.492 --> 43:41.327
Are you okay?

43:41.410 --> 43:43.912
In the middle of the night,
suddenly, like "wahh!"

44:48.227 --> 44:50.896
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.
